Highlight selected list options in saved appearances (MuPDF 1.28.6)

This file modifies MuPDF. The Mervin PDF project added this local fix on
2026-11-04. It is not an upstream backport. Remove it when the pinned release
renders selected list rows with the same coverage.

Read inherited /Opt, /TI, /V and /I. Match /V against export values, paint
display labels, and use /I when present to distinguish equal export values.
Combo boxes also paint display labels rather than export values.
Draw only visible rows, with white text on blue for each selected option.
Retain the widget background, border and rotation. Each row has its own
clipped Form XObject so long labels cannot wrap into another option and
Unicode fonts or shaped text do not replace other rows' resources.

This follows patch 0004. tests/tst_form_model.cpp checks saved appearances,
shared widgets, single and multiple selection, export/display pairs, top
indices, duplicate values, negative cases and raster differences.

